			<div class="content" id="post-content-1816844">
									

<p>This doesn't have to do with the D-class issue at all. &quot;Terminate&quot; is used as a bureaucratic euphemism <em>any</em> time the Foundation <em>deliberately</em> executes someone. Regardless of your position on whether the Foundation actually terminates D-classes at the end of the month, it still refers to a <em>deliberate action</em> the Foundation is taking, not the actions of an SCP object ending with someone dying. Therefore, it is always incorrect to refer to an SCP object's effects happening to kill someone as it &quot;terminating&quot; them.</p>

